  "faqSectionGettingStarted": "Getting Started",
  "faqWhatIsIntended": "What is Intended?",
  "faqWhatIsIntendedAnswer": "Intended is a gentle habit app for iOS. It helps you build daily habits without streaks, guilt, or pressure. There's no counter that resets when you miss a day — just a calm space to check in with your intentions whenever you're ready.",
  "faqWhatIsIntentionPath": "What's an Intention Path?",
  "faqWhatIsIntentionPathAnswer": "When you first open Intended, you choose a path based on what brings you here — like Finding Calm or Gentle Mornings. Your path shapes your default habits, the tone of your reminders, and your reflection questions. You can change it anytime in your profile.",
  "faqChangeIntentionPath": "Can I change my Intention Path?",
  "faqChangeIntentionPathAnswer": "Yes, anytime. Go to your Profile, tap your Intention Path card, and pick a new one. Your history and check-ins stay exactly as they are.",
  "faqWhatAreFocusAreas": "What are Focus Areas?",
  "faqWhatAreFocusAreasAnswer": "Focus areas are categories of habits — like Health, Mood, or Self-care. Each area comes with curated habits. Your path pre-selects a couple, but you can add or remove them anytime.",
  "faqHowIsDifferent": "How is Intended different?",
  "faqHowIsDifferentAnswer": "Most habit apps use streaks and gamification. Intended takes the opposite approach. No streaks to break, no leaderboards, no guilt. Your progress never resets.",
  "faqNeedAccount": "Do I need an account?",
  "faqNeedAccountAnswer": "Not to get started. You can use Intended without signing in. Creating an account (via Apple or Google) lets you back up your data to the cloud and restore it if you switch devices.",
  "faqSectionDailyHabits": "Daily Habits",
  "faqHowToCheckIn": "How do I check in?",
  "faqHowToCheckInAnswer": "Tap any habit card on your home screen. A single tap is all it takes.",
  "faqMissedDay": "What if I miss a day?",
  "faqMissedDayAnswer": "Nothing happens. No streaks break, no counters reset — research on habit formation found a missed day doesn't materially set you back. If you were quiet a few days, the first square after is marked as a return, not the gap as a failure. And if you did the thing but didn't log it: long-press the card to log yesterday.",
  "faqHowToPin": "How do I pin a habit?",
  "faqHowToPinAnswer": "Long-press any habit card to pin it to the top. You can have one pinned habit at a time.",
  "faqCustomHabits": "Can I add custom habits?",
  "faqCustomHabitsAnswer": "Yes! Tap the + button. Free users can have up to 2 custom habits. Intended+ gives you unlimited.",
  "faqSwapHabit": "How do I swap a habit?",
  "faqSwapHabitAnswer": "Tap the swap icon on any habit card. Free users get 2 swaps per month.",
  "faqRefreshes": "What are refreshes?",
  "faqRefreshesAnswer": "Refreshing gives you new random habits from your focus areas. 3 per day on the free plan.",
  "faqAllDone": "What happens when I complete all my habits?",
  "faqAllDoneAnswer": "You'll see a quiet celebration — a gentle bloom moment. It's a small reminder that showing up matters, no matter how many habits you checked off.",
  "faqSectionReflections": "Your month",
  "faqWeeklyReflection": "What is a Weekly Reflection?",
  "faqWeeklyReflectionAnswer": "Every week, Intended generates a reflection card based on your check-in patterns — which habits stuck, your most active days, and gentle observations. Never judgments.",
  "faqMonthlyReflection": "What's the Monthly Reflection?",
  "faqMonthlyReflectionAnswer": "After 30 days, a monthly reflection looks across weeks for patterns you might not notice day-to-day. Available with Intended+.",
  "faqShareReflection": "Can I share my reflection?",
  "faqShareReflectionAnswer": "Yes — on Your month, tap Share under your season. It becomes a story-sized card with your grid and your season word, sized for Instagram or TikTok. Habit names are never on it unless you put them there.",
  "faqNoReflection": "Why don't I see a reflection?",
  "faqNoReflectionAnswer": "Weekly reflections appear after 7 days. Monthly after 30. The more you check in, the richer they become.",
  "faqHowReflectionsGenerated": "How are reflections generated?",
  "faqHowReflectionsGeneratedAnswer": "Reflections are generated entirely on your device from your check-in data. No AI, no cloud processing. The app looks at your patterns — active days, favorite habits, consistency — and turns them into gentle observations.",
  "faqSectionNotifications": "Notifications",
  "faqHowNotifications": "How do notifications work?",
  "faqHowNotificationsAnswer": "Reminders adapt to your rhythm. Check in regularly and they step back. Been away? One gentle nudge — never seven.",
  "faqChangeTime": "Can I change the time?",
  "faqChangeTimeAnswer": "Yes. Profile → Notification Settings.",
  "faqPathNotifications": "Do notifications match my path?",
  "faqPathNotificationsAnswer": "Yes. Someone on Finding Calm sees different wording than someone on Gentle Mornings.",
  "faqTurnOffNotifications": "Can I turn off notifications?",
  "faqTurnOffNotificationsAnswer": "Yes. Go to Profile → Notification Settings and toggle them off. You can also disable just the weekly reflection reminder while keeping daily ones.",
  "faqSectionWidgets": "Widgets",
  "faqAddWidget": "How do I add a widget?",
  "faqAddWidgetAnswer": "Long-press your home screen, tap +, search for Intended. You can also add lock screen widgets through iOS Settings.",
  "faqWidgetNotUpdating": "Why isn't my widget updating?",
  "faqWidgetNotUpdatingAnswer": "iOS controls refresh timing. Open the app briefly to trigger it. Check that Background App Refresh is enabled for Intended.",
  "faqSectionPricing": "Intended+ & Pricing",
  "faqWhatIsPlus": "What is Intended+?",
  "faqWhatIsPlusAnswer": "Intended+ is the reading of your month: the drift warning before a quiet stretch, a four-line letter, next month's plan built from this month's evidence, what actually lifts you, the season's explanation and archive — plus all ten themes, premium icons and widgets.",
  "faqPricing": "How much does it cost?",
  "faqPricingAnswer": "Monthly: {monthly}. Yearly: {yearly}. Lifetime: {lifetime}, one-time. Both subscriptions start with a {days}-day free trial.",
